usage: csk audit [-h] [--all] [--global] [--json] [--allow CONTENT_SHA256]
                 [--reason REASON] [--publish RECORD] [--registry REGISTRY]
                 [--token TOKEN]
                 [target]

positional arguments:
  target                project alias, '.', or project path

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --all                 audit all registered projects and global skills
  --global              audit global skills
  --json                print machine-readable JSON
  --allow CONTENT_SHA256
                        pin a legacy content hash to satisfy strict schema
                        v1/v2 capability declaration checks
  --reason REASON       required reason for --allow
  --publish RECORD      submit a signed audit record (JSON file) to a registry
  --registry REGISTRY   registry base URL for --publish
  --token TOKEN         auditor token for --publish (or set
                        CSK_REGISTRY_TOKEN)

Scope:
  By default audits the current project. Use a target, --all, or --global for other scopes.
  --all audits registered projects and global skills.

Side effects:
  Read-only. Missing git URL sources may be cloned into temporary directories only.

Examples:
  csk audit
  csk audit . --json
  csk audit --all
  csk audit --global
